/-!
# The small marked MS configuration

`markedMS_of_source` constructs every MS hypothesis for (LS,S), the actual
V₂ constituent marking and the surviving A₆/G₂ blocks or C.1.34(1)–(3).
It retains SQTK with its catalogue and the precise earlier universal FF/MS
implications. The comparison excludes every incompatible C.1.32 model,
proves simplicity of L/O₂(L), and constructs its equivalence with L*
compatible with the original star map.

The output preserves the central submodules and dual actions, both
transported lines in the doubled-natural case, and the literal equality
[O₂(L),L] = [O₂(I),L]. The source's local alternatives and geometric
witnesses are derived, not assumed. The universal earlier classifications
remain explicit inputs; the parent owns the subsequent extension
calculation and the exclusion of this small branch in 15.3.31.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), proof of
15.3.31, printed p.1132 (PDF p.1149), using C.1.31–34, pp.135–137.
-/
